"""Render the audited qualification scorecard into repository documentation."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'artifacts/s1_arpae500'
load=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text())
q=load(OUT/'qualification.json');audit=load(OUT/'audit.json')
rows=[load(p) for p in sorted((OUT/'attempts').glob('*.json'))]
labels={'fixed':'None','tap':'Taps','shunt':'Shunts','tap_shunt':'Taps + shunts'}
lines=['# S1 500-bus qualification','','The 500-bus **fixed-droop** S1 study has independently verified feasible points for all **20 equipment-policy/demand contracts**. The matched matrix accepts **163/180 attempts**; retries remain separate. This is base-case steady-state qualification, not N−1 security or a global-optimality claim.','','## Model and frozen design','','The source is ARPA-E Challenge 1 Network Model 01, Scenario 02: 500 buses, 90 generator records (51 online), 599 branch records (593 online: 462 lines and 131 transformers), and 17 shunt-bank records (11 online). There are no fixed bus shunts in the source; line charging is retained separately. All original imported OPF/SCOPF results remain unchanged.','','Study limits are Pmin=0 and Qmin=−max(abs(original Qmin),abs(original Qmax)), with Qmax its positive counterpart. Source limits remain separately available. Every bus has Vmin=0.9 and Vmax=1.1 pu. All online branches have ratings; the range is 0.2–1350 MVA. Device-specific generator, angle, tap, shunt and flow limits are exported with each selected witness.','','A nominal joint loss OPF selects all 131 online taps within 0.95–1.05 and all 11 online banks within their own continuous B envelopes (Bmin=0, Bmax=0.3–1.0 pu depending on bank). These are study tap bounds, not confirmed OLTC hardware limits. Shunts are continuous susceptances, not discrete switching. The joint reference loses 17.581868 MW, compared with 18.101590 MW for the fixed-source-equipment loss OPF.','','Each of the 51 online generators receives a shifted-zero-Q, zero-deadband curve: m=0.08/(Qmax−Qmin), Vref=Vopf+m Qopf, Q(V)=clip((Vref−V)/m,Qmin,Qmax). Slopes use pu voltage per pu Q on the 100 MVA system base. Curves are calibrated once at nominal demand. The precursor replay verifies every curve at its reference, with maximum exact-droop residual 7.69e−15 pu. All curves and nominal equipment settings are frozen for the no-free-control arm. Demand-matched loss/cost OPFs change initialization only.','','## Scope: free-droop studies remain pending','','This campaign qualifies the frozen 8% curves carried forward from the 14-bus decision; it varies only equipment freedom. It does not complete the full S1 control-design matrix. Free-droop-only, droop+tap, droop+shunt and droop+tap+shunt arms have not been run. That is a scope omission, not a solver limitation or evidence against droop optimization.','','The next design comparison should distinguish slope-only optimization from slope-plus-Vref optimization, state each parameter bound, and initially keep deadband zero. After design, freeze each candidate and recheck all demand points with the same precursor and feasibility gates. Independently refitting curves at every demand is a separate adaptive-design benchmark and must not be reported as one robust fixed design.','','## Matched matrix and recovered performance','','Each cell has three OPF-derived starts (nominal joint, demand-matched loss, demand-matched cost) and three solvers (Ipopt, MadNLP, CCOpt): nine direct attempts. Direct budgets are 1,000 iterations/60 solver seconds (Ipopt CPU-time limit; MadNLP/CCOpt wall-time limits). Measured solve wall time can also include first-use compilation; this is not a strictly matched wall-time speed benchmark. No flat starts are used. Free-equipment arms preserve the same curves and freeze unselected equipment at the joint reference.','','Losses below are the best accepted local solutions found, including separately recorded recovery/continuation. Direct acceptance counts are never replaced by retry results.','','| Free equipment | Direct accepted | 90% loss MW | 95% | 100% | 105% | 110% |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for family,label in labels.items():
 rs=[r for r in q['scorecard'] if r['family']==family]
 lines.append('| '+label+' | '+str(sum(r['direct_accepted'] for r in rs))+'/45 | '+' | '.join(f"{r['loss_mw']:.6f}" for r in rs)+' |')
fixed90=next(r for r in q['scorecard'] if r['family']=='fixed' and r['factor']==.9)
free90=next(r for r in q['scorecard'] if r['family']=='tap_shunt' and r['factor']==.9)
lines += ['',f"At 90% demand, freeing both equipment families reduces the best-found losses by {100*(1-free90['loss_mw']/fixed90['loss_mw']):.1f}%, but increases evaluated source economic cost from {fixed90['economic_cost']:.2f} to {free90['economic_cost']:.2f} ({100*(free90['economic_cost']/fixed90['economic_cost']-1):.1f}%). This is a loss-minimizing comparison, not a cost-optimal dispatch recommendation."]
lines+=['','## Verification and headroom','','Acceptance requires successful native solver termination **and** independent physical replay. The three-outcome model gate remains feasible / certified infeasible / unresolved. A native failure on a model with an independently verified witness is a solver failure; it is not an infeasibility certificate. All 20 primary contracts are feasible.','','Physical tolerances are unchanged: AC balance 1e−6 pu, exact droop 1e−5 pu, equipment/network limits 1e−6 pu, control settings 1e−8, and angles 1e−6 rad. Smooth solves use 1e−6 pu voltage and Q smoothing; CCOpt uses complementarity. Independently recomputed losses, economic costs, exact droop and both-end branch flows determine acceptance.','','| Demand, fixed equipment | Best loss MW | Minimum upper voltage margin pu | Maximum branch loading % | Solvers with an accepted loss witness after retries |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for r in q['scorecard']:
 if r['family']=='fixed':lines.append(f"| {r['factor']:.0%} | {r['loss_mw']:.6f} | {r['minimum_voltage_upper_margin_pu']:.3g} | {r['maximum_branch_loading_percent']:.3f} | {', '.join(r['solvers_with_loss_witness'])} |")
lines+=['','Voltage ceilings and some generator bounds are binding; feasible does not mean comfortable headroom. At the nominal reference the highest branch loading is 56.14% (branch 299, 112.276/200 MVA). The smallest absolute margin, 0.14009 MVA on line 30 rated 0.2 MVA, is not the most stressed branch in percentage terms. Do not interpret the sampled demand points as continuous-range robustness or dynamic stability. The cost column in raw results is the source piecewise-linear economic cost evaluated at the point; the downstream objective here is active loss.','','## Failure stress tests','','The complete generated table is `artifacts/s1_arpae500/FAILED_COMBINATIONS.md`, with machine-readable evidence in `failed_combinations.json`. It lists all 43 direct failed solver/model/demand combinations and all 61 unsuccessful attempts including retries. Recovery requires the same solver, loss objective and constraints; changed-equipment fixes are labelled separately. Regenerate with `python3 examples/report_s1_arpae500_failures.py`.','','All unsuccessful attempts are retained in `artifacts/s1_arpae500/REPORT.md` and `failure_diagnostics.json`. Smooth-solver direct failures and all free-equipment failures were recovered using independently verified points on the same model. CCOpt required additional light-load tests: verified starts, 3,000 iterations/120 seconds, constant-objective feasibility, and smaller initial barrier/bound push with unchanged tolerances. Both 90% and 95% CCOpt loss solves recovered from smooth-solver witnesses with smaller initial barrier (1e−6 and 1e−8 respectively) and bound push/fraction 1e−8; all three solvers now have accepted loss witnesses at all five fixed-equipment demands. See `ccopt_fix` rows for the retained failed retries; a constant-objective pass proves feasibility but is not a loss-optimal result.','','The failed CCOpt light-load points expose relaxed voltage-hinge errors amplified by inverse droop slope. At generator 14/bus 9 a failed 95% run had about 0.00071 pu voltage-hinge error and 6.38 MVAr exact-droop error. Another constant-objective point satisfies the physical equations despite a native locally-infeasible status; it is retained as a physical witness without being counted as solver acceptance. The historical campaign left the library formulation unchanged and recommended eliminating redundant zero-deadband voltage hinges. That specialization and its explicit equivalence tests are now implemented; the separately scored [numerical follow-up](s1_zero_deadband.md) records 11/12 primary replays and 12/12 combinations after one bounded retry.','','All 20 downward continuation steps from 100% to 90% in 0.5-percentage-point increments passed. They reproduce the approximately 33.0725 MW loss at 90% and 26.5676 MW at 95%, without improving the best solutions already found. This is a local-minimum stress test, not proof of global optimality. It preserves the curves and equipment; intermediate points do not recalibrate the design. Original-P, original-Q and combined original-bound overlays are separate stress contracts, retaining the exact study-calibrated curves. Their outcomes are recorded below.','','| Original-bound overlay | Accepted source cost OPFs | Accepted droop attempts (direct) | Fixed-equipment demand points with verified witnesses | Free-tap/shunt fix: verified demands |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for family in ('original_p','original_q','original_pq'):
 source=[r for r in rows if r['tags']['stage']=='original_source' and r['tags']['family']==family]
 direct=[r for r in rows if r['tags']['stage']=='original_limits' and r['tags']['family']==family]
 allr=[r for r in rows if r['tags'].get('family')==family and r['tags']['stage'] in ('original_limits','recovery')]
 fixes=[r for r in rows if r['tags']['stage']=='original_equipment_fix' and r['tags']['family']==family]
 fix_count=str(len({r['tags']['factor'] for r in fixes if r['point_pass']}))+'/5' if fixes else '—'
 lines.append(f"| {family} | {sum(r['accepted'] for r in source)}/{len(source)} | {sum(r['accepted'] for r in direct)}/{len(direct)} | {len({r['tags']['factor'] for r in allr if r['point_pass']})}/5 | {fix_count} |")
lines+=['','Restoring original Pmin alone is feasible at all five demands, with all three solver lanes recovered. Restoring original Q bounds, with or without Pmin, has no verified frozen-equipment point in these tests (30 direct local failures). These cases remain **unresolved**, not globally certified infeasible. A 30-second/15-round sparse outer-LP test at each demand retained droop graphs and conservative necessary voltage bounds derived from exact curve-knot inversion; it found no infeasibility certificate. Results and derivations are saved separately.','','At nominal demand, a representative failed original-Q point satisfies AC balance and operating bounds but generator 1 at bus 223 has about −0.88 MVAr output while its fixed curve requests −2.34 MVAr (1.46 MVAr mismatch). The original-Q cap narrows admissible controller-bus voltages, so the study-selected frozen equipment cannot be assumed compatible. This is a diagnosis of the failed points, not a proof that every frozen-equipment point is impossible.','','**Tested fix:** free all 131 taps within 0.95–1.05 and all 11 continuous banks within their original study envelopes, while keeping the study curves and restored generator limits. All ten original-Q/original-PQ demand contracts pass with Ipopt. This changes equipment freedom and is explicitly separate from the unresolved frozen-equipment contracts. Recalibration using original limits is another potential design change, not tested here.','','Use original reactive limits during reference construction if they will be required in deployment; otherwise retain the requested symmetric-Q study label. Do not silently substitute a free-equipment witness for a frozen-design qualification.']
lines+=['','## Evidence and reproduction','',f"The final audit replayed **{audit['states_replayed']} saved states**, with **zero discrepancies**, and confirmed preserved source OPF/SCOPF hashes. A separate standard-library Python replay independently recomputed AC flows/balance, physical limits, exact droop and original-limit overlays for all saved states, also with zero classification discrepancies. Full per-device values and thresholds are in `artifacts/s1_arpae500/thresholds/`; selected states/policies are in `demand_witnesses.json`. Every attempt carries a case/policy fingerprint and initialization/solver/objective/budget contract. `protocol.json` preserves initial provenance, and `final_code_manifest.json` records final runner versions.",'','Run from the repository root, in order. These runners are S1-only and checkpoint/resume identical contracts:','','```sh','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_campaign.jl reference','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_campaign.jl frozen','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_equipment.jl','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_recovery.jl','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_ccopt_fix.jl','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_continuation.jl','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_original_limits.jl','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_recovery.jl','julia --project=. examples/s1_arpae500_original_diagnostic.jl',
'julia --project=. examples/audit_s1_arpae500.jl',
'python3 examples/audit_s1_arpae500_independent.py','julia --project=. examples/diagnose_s1_arpae500.jl','python3 examples/report_s1_arpae500.py','python3 examples/finalize_s1_arpae500.py','python3 examples/report_s1_arpae500_qualification.py','```','','The optional certificate runner is `examples/s1_arpae500_original_certificate.jl`; its pinned HiGHS environment and exact depot used are recorded in `protocol.json` and `global_environment/`. No new solver dependencies were installed.\n\nUse the frozen design as the reproducible baseline and the free-equipment arms as performance comparisons. Preserve solver-specific failures and avoid selecting a policy solely by its best loss. Any security study is a separate S2/SCOPF campaign, requiring confirmation of taps/shunts, timing and movement budgets under `AGENTS.md`. See the [execution plan](s1_500_plan.md) and [14-bus closeout](s1_14bus_closeout.md).','']
(ROOT/'docs/src/s1_500_results.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
print('Updated docs/src/s1_500_results.md')

# Preserve the separately scored zero-deadband numerical follow-up.
from s1_zero_deadband_reporting import append_followup
append_followup(ROOT/'docs/src/s1_500_results.md', doc=True)
